{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair","id":821510,"title":"Questions about the Lair","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-02T02:21:48-08:00","id":821510,"title":"Questions about the Lair","content":"I'm still a little confused by the explanations of the way that the Lair's Heart and Chambers are set up. Are they all set up in the same landscape (i.e. would a desert Lair's Chambers rise from the sand like ancient ruins) or are they completely separate, miniature worlds whose only connection is their Lair Traits? Do Lair Traits apply to all the Heart and all Chambers equally or does each Chamber have one attendant Lair Trait and it's only the Heart that has all of them? <br /> <br /> If I could get some answers it would be great. Thanks for reading (and hopefully answering).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T03:04:49-08:00","id":821523,"title":"","content":"The chambers are sort of mashed together in any way you want. It really depends on how the burrows are arranged. As for traits, I think beasts can switch them on and off at will, at least on a functional level. Whether this takes away the physical manifestation or not will probably depend on the chamber. A flooded cave might simply allow guests to breathe underwater, but an abandoned library might see the water coming and going. <br /> <br /> Whatever seems most thematic, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T05:12:40-08:00","id":821553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821523#post821523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The chambers are sort of mashed together in any way you want. It really depends on how the burrows are arranged. As for traits, I think beasts can switch them on and off at will, at least on a functional level. Whether this takes away the physical manifestation or not will probably depend on the chamber. A flooded cave might simply allow guests to breathe underwater, but an abandoned library might see the water coming and going.<br /> <br /> Whatever seems most thematic, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:53:35-08:00","id":821617,"title":"","content":"Have you seen much of the Nightmare on Elm Street series? <br /> <br /> It doesn't translate perfectly, but imagine the Boiler Room as the Heart of Freddy's Lair. The Elm Street House (1428 Elm Street) that once belonged to Nancy and her family is ultimately claimed as a Chamber. Both house and boiler room seem old and dilapidated, and both are twisted by strange dream-logic, and if you're in the Dream World, you can get from one to the other, but they are distinct locations. At some point -- likely during or possibly shortly after Nightmare 3, the Westin Hills Asylum probably becomes a new Chamber in Freddy's Lair. Each location is part of Freddy's Dream World. Each location has been changed by Freddy's presence. A Lair will work much the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:50:55-08:00","id":821649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair#post821510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still a little confused by the explanations of the way that the Lair's Heart and Chambers are set up. Are they all set up in the same landscape (i.e. would a desert Lair's Chambers rise from the sand like ancient ruins) or are they completely separate, miniature worlds whose only connection is their Lair Traits? Do Lair Traits apply to all the Heart and all Chambers equally or does each Chamber have one attendant Lair Trait and it's only the Heart that has all of them?<br /> <br /> If I could get some answers it would be great. Thanks for reading (and hopefully answering).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have these questions too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821617#post821617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen much of the Nightmare on Elm Street series?<br /> <br /> It doesn't translate perfectly, but imagine the Boiler Room as the Heart of Freddy's Lair. The Elm Street House (1428 Elm Street) that once belonged to Nancy and her family is ultimately claimed as a Chamber. Both house and boiler room seem old and dilapidated, and both are twisted by strange dream-logic, and if you're in the Dream World, you can get from one to the other, but they are distinct locations. At some point -- likely during or possibly shortly after Nightmare 3, the Westin Hills Asylum probably becomes a new Chamber in Freddy's Lair. Each location is part of Freddy's Dream World. Each location has been changed by Freddy's presence. A Lair will work much the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly I haven't seen these movies. Probably should, but can you give me a short run down. Is each &quot;chamber&quot; it's own unique place with it's own traits.<br /> <br /> For example my heart chamber let's say it's a frozen mountain top, with the traits Blizard and Extreme cold.<br /> Then I witness a werewolf go ballistic in a costco, using my Atavisms I managed to escape the slaughter but this Costco is now a lair of mine. While the Extreme cold trait would work, obviously blizzards don't happen indoors. So what happens here? Does the Blizzard trait drop from that room and one unique to that room pick up, and does this chamber look like a twisted Version of the Costco, or does it's appearance look like it fits in with the mountain. Like an Ice Cave in the mountain that blows in snow from the Blizzard outside. What is happening here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:05:55-08:00","id":821702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821649#post821649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have these questions too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever is the most narratively convenient means to connect each Chamber. While they are more or less part of the same &quot;layer&quot; of the Primordial Dream, the individual Chambers link to the Heart in a way that is narratively appropriate. So, if your desert Lair incorporates chambers built from a tomb complex, a convenience store, and a playground, for example, and your lair traits are Exposed, Blinding Light, and Sealed Exits, you might link each Chamber by mirage, and have the Pathways work by dead-reckoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821649#post821649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly I haven't seen these movies. Probably should, but can you give me a short run down. Is each &quot;chamber&quot; it's own unique place with it's own traits.<br /> <br /> For example my heart chamber let's say it's a frozen mountain top, with the traits Blizard and Extreme cold.<br /> Then I witness a werewolf go ballistic in a costco, using my Atavisms I managed to escape the slaughter but this Costco is now a lair of mine. While the Extreme cold trait would work, obviously blizzards don't happen indoors. So what happens here? Does the Blizzard trait drop from that room and one unique to that room pick up, and does this chamber look like a twisted Version of the Costco, or does it's appearance look like it fits in with the mountain. Like an Ice Cave in the mountain that blows in snow from the Blizzard outside. What is happening here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you're going for dream logic, open them freezer cases. Most frozen food in a warehouse store is kept in large, self-contained, walk-in refrigeration units, so a narratively plausible, if physically impractical explanation is readily at hand. Dreamworlds are places of sharps and flats, not banal adherence to realism. Now, if you're planning on using those traits in a waking-world fight, access to said walk-in freezer is quite helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:40:16-08:00","id":821762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821702#post821702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whatever is the most narratively convenient means to connect each Chamber. While they are more or less part of the same &amp;quot;layer&amp;quot; of the Primordial Dream, the individual Chambers link to the Heart in a way that is narratively appropriate. So, if your desert Lair incorporates chambers built from a tomb complex, a convenience store, and a playground, for example, and your lair traits are Exposed, Blinding Light, and Sealed Exits, you might link each Chamber by mirage, and have the Pathways work by dead-reckoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if you're going for dream logic, open them freezer cases. Most frozen food in a warehouse store is kept in large, self-contained, walk-in refrigeration units, so a narratively plausible, if physically impractical explanation is readily at hand. Dreamworlds are places of sharps and flats, not banal adherence to realism. Now, if you're planning on using those traits in a waking-world fight, access to said walk-in freezer is quite helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot for clearing this up. It's a great help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T23:21:26-08:00","id":823105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=821649#post821649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have these questions too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sadly I haven't seen these movies. Probably should, but can you give me a short run down. Is each &quot;chamber&quot; it's own unique place with it's own traits.<br /> <br /> For example my heart chamber let's say it's a frozen mountain top, with the traits Blizard and Extreme cold.<br /> Then I witness a werewolf go ballistic in a costco, using my Atavisms I managed to escape the slaughter but this Costco is now a lair of mine. While the Extreme cold trait would work, obviously blizzards don't happen indoors. So what happens here? Does the Blizzard trait drop from that room and one unique to that room pick up, and does this chamber look like a twisted Version of the Costco, or does it's appearance look like it fits in with the mountain. Like an Ice Cave in the mountain that blows in snow from the Blizzard outside. What is happening here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, you have two options. The first is a &quot;meta&quot; theme to the Lair. One Chamber (probably, but not necessarily the Heart Chamber) supplies a unifying theme to all the Burrows, with the other Chambers being a deviation.<br /> <br /> For example, the meta-theme for one Lair might be the Creepy Old Mansion. All the Burrows look like hallways: full of spooky portraits, dilapidated furniture, and cobwebs. Entries (from the Burrow) to a Chamber look like a doorway leading off the hallway. Step through the doorway, and you're in the Chamber, which may look nothing like the mansion: desert oasis, sunken pirate ship, volcano . . . And the access point to the Burrow/hallway might look <i>very</i> different, from within the Chamber.<br /> <br /> (The Beast could also 'hide&quot; Chambers, by making the entry point less obvious. You might access one hidden Chamber by stepping into a scenic painting, or walking through a full body mirror)<br /> <br /> The second is to give each Burrow a unique feel, merging elements from the two Chambers it connects, forming a seamless transition between the two (at least according to dream logic). Take your Costco/mountain Lair. <b>Hexmeister Vic </b>offers one good solution - the Burrow links through the walk-in freezer. As you head back through the freezer, dodging stacks of frozen peas and hanging slabs of beef, the floor and walls become irregular. You start getting more ice and snow, and less groceries. Finally, you're walking through an ice cave, just before you emerge out onto the frozen mountain.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could put the Burrow in the ceiling of the Costco. One of the acoustic panels in the drop-down ceiling feels a bit cold. Push it to the side, and snow falls down. Climb up into the ceiling . . . and you come out on the mountaintop.<br /> <br /> I suppose with the right Beast (and Lair), you could do &quot;warp points&quot;, or go down pipes (<i>a la</i> Super Mario), or . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit:</u></i> Oh, and don't be afraid to adapt Lair traits as necessary. &quot;Blizzard&quot; in the Costco could allow the Beast to turn the sprinklers on and off at will, or send the food flying off the shelves, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 02-04-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T02:47:06-08:00","id":823186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=823105#post823105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, you have two options. The first is a &quot;meta&quot; theme to the Lair. One Chamber (probably, but not necessarily the Heart Chamber) supplies a unifying theme to all the Burrows, with the other Chambers being a deviation.<br /> <br /> For example, the meta-theme for one Lair might be the Creepy Old Mansion. All the Burrows look like hallways: full of spooky portraits, dilapidated furniture, and cobwebs. Entries (from the Burrow) to a Chamber look like a doorway leading off the hallway. Step through the doorway, and you're in the Chamber, which may look nothing like the mansion: desert oasis, sunken pirate ship, volcano . . . And the access point to the Burrow/hallway might look <i>very</i> different, from within the Chamber.<br /> <br /> (The Beast could also 'hide&quot; Chambers, by making the entry point less obvious. You might access one hidden Chamber by stepping into a scenic painting, or walking through a full body mirror)<br /> <br /> The second is to give each Burrow a unique feel, merging elements from the two Chambers it connects, forming a seamless transition between the two (at least according to dream logic). Take your Costco/mountain Lair. <b>Hexmeister Vic </b>offers one good solution - the Burrow links through the walk-in freezer. As you head back through the freezer, dodging stacks of frozen peas and hanging slabs of beef, the floor and walls become irregular. You start getting more ice and snow, and less groceries. Finally, you're walking through an ice cave, just before you emerge out onto the frozen mountain.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could put the Burrow in the ceiling of the Costco. One of the acoustic panels in the drop-down ceiling feels a bit cold. Push it to the side, and snow falls down. Climb up into the ceiling . . . and you come out on the mountaintop.<br /> <br /> I suppose with the right Beast (and Lair), you could do &quot;warp points&quot;, or go down pipes (<i>a la</i> Super Mario), or . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit:</u></i> Oh, and don't be afraid to adapt Lair traits as necessary. &quot;Blizzard&quot; in the Costco could allow the Beast to turn the sprinklers on and off at will, or send the food flying off the shelves, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm imagining a Burrow being like the wardrobe in The Lion, The Witch and the Wardrobe. Except this isn't Narnia...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T03:17:38-08:00","id":823196,"title":"","content":"Yes. Perfect. That's exactly what they're like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T06:43:46-08:00","id":823294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821510-questions-about-the-lair?p=823105#post823105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, you have two options. The first is a &quot;meta&quot; theme to the Lair. One Chamber (probably, but not necessarily the Heart Chamber) supplies a unifying theme to all the Burrows, with the other Chambers being a deviation.<br /> <br /> For example, the meta-theme for one Lair might be the Creepy Old Mansion. All the Burrows look like hallways: full of spooky portraits, dilapidated furniture, and cobwebs. Entries (from the Burrow) to a Chamber look like a doorway leading off the hallway. Step through the doorway, and you're in the Chamber, which may look nothing like the mansion: desert oasis, sunken pirate ship, volcano . . . And the access point to the Burrow/hallway might look <i>very</i> different, from within the Chamber.<br /> <br /> (The Beast could also 'hide&quot; Chambers, by making the entry point less obvious. You might access one hidden Chamber by stepping into a scenic painting, or walking through a full body mirror)<br /> <br /> The second is to give each Burrow a unique feel, merging elements from the two Chambers it connects, forming a seamless transition between the two (at least according to dream logic). Take your Costco/mountain Lair. <b>Hexmeister Vic </b>offers one good solution - the Burrow links through the walk-in freezer. As you head back through the freezer, dodging stacks of frozen peas and hanging slabs of beef, the floor and walls become irregular. You start getting more ice and snow, and less groceries. Finally, you're walking through an ice cave, just before you emerge out onto the frozen mountain.<br /> <br /> Alternately, you could put the Burrow in the ceiling of the Costco. One of the acoustic panels in the drop-down ceiling feels a bit cold. Push it to the side, and snow falls down. Climb up into the ceiling . . . and you come out on the mountaintop.<br /> <br /> I suppose with the right Beast (and Lair), you could do &quot;warp points&quot;, or go down pipes (<i>a la</i> Super Mario), or . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit:</u></i> Oh, and don't be afraid to adapt Lair traits as necessary. &quot;Blizzard&quot; in the Costco could allow the Beast to turn the sprinklers on and off at will, or send the food flying off the shelves, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhh okay.<br /> When I first read about chambers in the Lair I thought (For the sake of simplicity we will continue the Costco example with the Ice Mountain Heart) that each chamber became a part of that theme. I rather like what you said. It makes sense to me. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T08:40:46-08:00","id":823383,"title":"","content":"Lairs operate on Dream Logic, so there's a lot of leeway. I know I've had plenty of dreams where I'm walking around a familiar place and suddenly it just *isn't* anymore, and the transition felt perfectly smooth in the dream but there's no way to make sense of it after I wake up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}